{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The maximum magnitude outcome for each lottery is the largest absolute value outcome: for Lottery A, it is -3000 Euros (absolute value 3000), and for Lottery B, it is -6000 Euros (absolute value 6000). The probabilities of these outcomes are 0.2% for A and 0.1% for B. The reason evaluates which lottery has the more favorable (i.e., less negative) maximum magnitude outcome, weighted by its probability. Here, the weighted maximum magnitude outcomes are: A: 3000 × 0.002 = 6, B: 6000 × 0.001 = 6. The weighted magnitudes are equal, so the reason would be indifferent between A and B, or possibly lean toward A if considering the smaller loss as more favorable despite equal weighting.",
